<title>FRANCE: Sema Group wins Britain's NATS contract.</title>
<headline>Sema Group wins Britain's NATS contract.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-06-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Franco-British electronics and computer services company Sema Group Plc said on Tuesday that it won a contract to manage the Information Management Systems of Britain's National Air Traffic Services (NATS). The value of the contract was not disclosed.</p>
<p>Sema group said in a statement the initial four-year phase of the contract had the potential to be extended up to 10 years.</p>
<p>Industry sources put the value of the four-year contract at around 20 million stg.</p>
<p>-- Paris newsroom +331 4221 5432</p>
</text>
